# The autoplayer's helm, as a behaviour tree.
#
# WHY. `auto_player_console.mast` runs five `await delay_sim(n)` + `jump` loops per ship,
# hooked per console - so N connected clients hook every ship N times, five labels each
# start with their own `->END if ship is None`, and a supervisor re-polls every 5 seconds
# to re-hook respawns. A brain gets one tree per AGENT, automatic unscheduling when the
# ship dies, `__BRAIN_PAUSED__` while it is parked on the standby list, RollingSlicer
# pacing instead of a per-ship timer, and a live view of what it decided in the
# `brain_scan` console tab - none of which a loop gets.
#
# THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL ASKED FOR. `AUTO_PLAY.brain` defaults to false, so the existing
# console autoplayer is untouched and this can be A/B'd against it by flipping one
# setting on the same map and seed. That is deliberately reversible: the loop version is
# a working attract mode and should not be replaced on assertion.
#
# HOW A LEAF MUST BEHAVE - the one rule that is not obvious. Each leaf is ONE synchronous
# pass ending in `yield success` or `yield fail`. It must never `await`: an awaiting leaf
# is left running while the brain starts another next pass. (The library now ends such a
# leaf and says so once, rather than leaking a task per pass forever - but the leaf still
# has to be written this way to mean anything.) Work that takes time goes in a
# `task_schedule`d label gated by a flag, which is what the weapons opener already does.
#
# THE ENERGY REFILL IS GONE, on purpose. The loop version tops the tank up at `energy < 30`
# so an unattended run would not stall - and that also hides every real energy bug behind
# it. It is replaced by `ai_player_recover_energy`, which is competence rather than a
# cheat: the tank drains ONLY while the throttle is up and the auxiliary power unit refills
# it unconditionally below its ceiling, so stopping always recovers. There is no
# unrecoverable energy state; a ship that strands is one that never stopped burning.

# Hook every player ship once, when the game starts. //shared/signal, not //signal: this
# is server-side work and must happen ONCE, not once per connected console - which is the
# duplication the loop version has to live with.
//shared/signal/game_started if SETTINGS.get("AUTO_PLAY", {}).get("brain")
    await delay_sim(2)
    # `brain` WINS over `enable`: an explicit ask for the tree should get the tree. The
    # loop version's own gate stands it down, so the two can never drive at once.
    task_schedule(ap_brain_attach_all)


=== ap_brain_attach_all
" Attach the helm brain to every player ship, and to any that respawn later.
metadata: ``` yaml
brain:
  SEQ:
    - SEL:
        - ai_player_flee_black_hole
        - ai_player_recover_energy
        - ai_player_dock
        - ai_player_hold_if_crippled
        - ai_player_pursue
        - ai_player_wander
    - ai_player_science_select
    - ai_player_comms
    - ai_player_weapons_doctrine
    - ai_player_engineer_power
```
    # The tree is declared as metadata rather than a MAST dict literal, which is the form
    # every prefab already uses (see prefabs/basic_enemy.mast). It is also the only safe
    # one: MAST parses line by line, so a `{...}` spanning lines is an unclosed brace that
    # desyncs the compiler for the rest of the file - and a story that does not compile
    # runs zero labels while still reporting PASS. YAML in a metadata block has no such
    # problem.
    #
    # A respawned ship is a NEW id with no `__BRAIN__`, so this still needs a watcher -
    # the brain system unschedules a dead agent for us but cannot know about its
    # replacement. Cheaper than the loop version's supervisor, which re-checked five
    # hooks per ship; here one inventory key answers it.
---apba_loop
    for ap_ship in to_object_list(role("__player__")):
        if not ap_ship.get_inventory_value("AP_BRAIN_HOOKED", False):
            ap_ship.set_inventory_value("AP_BRAIN_HOOKED", True)
            ap_ship.set_inventory_value("MANUAL_BEAMS_ON", True)
            brain_add(ap_ship.id, brain)
            # SAY WHICH AUTOPLAYER IS DRIVING, somewhere a person will actually see it.
            # `log(msg, "autoplay")` was the obvious choice and is useless: it goes to a
            # named logger with no handler configured, so it goes nowhere at all. The only
            # other tell was the brain_scan tab, which needs a dev build. comms_broadcast
            # reaches the text waterfall AND the ship's Log panel on any console.
            comms_broadcast(ap_ship.id, "Autopilot: behaviour tree engaged (AUTO_PLAY.brain)", color="#8cf")
            ap_ship.set_inventory_value("ap_driver", "brain")
    await delay_sim(5)
    jump apba_loop


# ---- the leaves, in priority order -------------------------------------------------
# The root is a SEQUENCE, so every console runs each pass. Inside it the HELM is a
# Select, where the first leaf that succeeds owns the ship - so within the helm, order is
# the policy. Each leaf opens with the conditions under which it declines.
#
# A Select root would have been wrong here and silently so: the helm succeeds on almost
# every pass, which would starve science, comms, weapons and engineering forever.

=== ai_player_flee_black_hole
" Fleeing a black hole
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
margin: 2000
throttle: 3.0
```
    # Highest priority: a hole PULLS, so the danger zone is its gravity_radius rather than
    # the small kill radius. Mines are NOT fled - they are threaded further down, because
    # fleeing a ring of them means bouncing off it forever and never docking.
    ap_hole = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, role("black_hole"), 15000))
    yield fail if ap_hole is None
    ap_gr = ap_hole.data_set.get("gravity_radius", 0) or 5000
    yield fail if sbs.distance_id(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, to_id(ap_hole)) >= ap_gr + margin

    ap_away = BRAIN_AGENT.pos - ap_hole.pos
    if ap_away.length() < 1:
        ap_away = Vec3(1, 0, 0)
    helm_steer_to_vec(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_away)
    helm_throttle(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, throttle)
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "flee")
    yield success


=== ai_player_recover_energy
" Recovering energy
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
reserve: 400
```
    # REPLACES THE REFILL CHEAT. Below the reserve, stop burning: the auxiliary power unit
    # refills the tank unconditionally, so a stopped ship always recovers. Docking is
    # faster, so prefer it when a friendly station is close enough to be worth the trip -
    # `helm_energy_reserve` asks whether we can afford to GET there, which a flat "energy
    # below 300" cannot express (300 says nothing about a station 40,000 units away).
    yield fail if helm_energy_reserve(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, reserve=reserve)

    ap_base = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, side_allied_members(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "station")))
    if ap_base is not None and helm_energy_reserve(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_base, reserve=0):
        helm_steer_to_point(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_base)
        helm_throttle(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, 1.0, allow_warp=False)
        if sbs.distance_id(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, to_id(ap_base)) < 700:
            helm_dock_request(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_base)
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "refuel")
        yield success

    # Nothing reachable: hold still and let the APU do it. Slow, certain, and honest -
    # if this is not enough the run has found something worth knowing.
    helm_stop(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "regen")
    yield success


=== ai_player_dock
" Docking to repair
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
shield_low: 0.3
undock_energy: 1000
```
    # Hysteresis, or the ship oscillates on the threshold: once committed we stay docked
    # until BOTH shields are full and the tank is well past the trigger.
    ap_docking = BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("ap_go_dock", False)
    ap_front = helm_shield_fraction(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, 0)
    ap_rear = helm_shield_fraction(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, 1)

    if ap_docking:
        if ap_front >= 1.0 and ap_rear >= 1.0 and helm_energy(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) >= undock_energy:
            BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_go_dock", False)
            helm_undock(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
            yield fail
    else:
        yield fail if ap_front >= shield_low and ap_rear >= shield_low
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_go_dock", True)

    ap_base = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, side_allied_members(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "station")))
    yield fail if ap_base is None
    yield success if helm_is_docked(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)

    helm_steer_to_point(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_base)
    ap_range = sbs.distance_id(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, to_id(ap_base))
    if ap_range < 700:
        helm_dock_request(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_base)
    else:
        helm_throttle(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, autoplay_helm_speed_for(ap_range))
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "dock")
    yield success


=== ai_player_hold_if_crippled
" Holding station - cannot steer
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
```
    # A straight-line burn with no steering just flies us into deep space chasing
    # something we cannot aim at. Hold until the maneuver system recovers.
    yield fail if helm_can_turn(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    helm_stop(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "hold")
    yield success


=== ai_player_pursue
" Pursuing a target
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
close_range: 10000
upgrade_range: 5000
wreck_range: 7500
```
    # Priority within pursuit: a close hostile first, then loot, then the far hostile.
    # `side_hostile_ships` is diplomacy-based, so a ceasefired clan or a surrendered ship
    # is not chased.
    ap_foes = side_hostile_ships(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    ap_target = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_foes, close_range))
    if ap_target is None:
        ap_target = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, all_roles("upgrade"), upgrade_range))
    if ap_target is None:
        ap_target = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, all_roles("wreck"), wreck_range))
    if ap_target is None:
        ap_target = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_foes))
    yield fail if ap_target is None

    ap_diff = ap_target.pos - BRAIN_AGENT.pos
    ap_range = ap_diff.length()
    ap_speed = autoplay_helm_speed_for(ap_range)

    # Standoff: the weapons opener asks us to hold at a range so its EMP/Nuke do not
    # detonate point-blank.
    ap_standoff = BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("weapons_standoff", 0) or 0
    if ap_standoff > 0 and is_hostile_combatant(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_target):
        if ap_range <= ap_standoff:
            ap_speed = 0
        elif ap_range <= ap_standoff + 2000:
            ap_speed = 0.5

    # Mines: cap speed early so there is room to steer, then bend the course around them
    # rather than fleeing - a station ringed by mines has to stay reachable.
    ap_steer = ap_diff
    ap_mine = to_object(closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, any_role("mine,maelstrom"), 8000))
    if ap_mine is not None:
        ap_md = sbs.distance_id(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, to_id(ap_mine))
        ap_speed = autoplay_helm_mine_cap(ap_speed, ap_md)
        ap_steer = autoplay_helm_deflect(BRAIN_AGENT.pos, ap_mine.pos, ap_diff, ap_md)
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "mine_slow")
    else:
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "pursue")

    helm_steer_to_vec(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_steer)
    helm_throttle(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_speed)
    yield success


=== ai_player_wander
" Roaming
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
repick_within: 2000
```
    # Anti-degeneracy: with nothing to chase, roam so attract never looks frozen on a
    # lobby screen. Last in the Select, so it only runs when everything else declined.
    ap_wander = BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("wander_target", None)
    if ap_wander is None or (ap_wander - BRAIN_AGENT.pos).length() < repick_within:
        ap_wander = Vec3.rand_in_sphere(8000, 25000, False, True)
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("wander_target", ap_wander)
    helm_steer_to_point(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_wander)
    # Do not wander with no steering - that is a one-way trip into deep space.
    helm_throttle(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, 1.0 if helm_can_turn(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) else 0)
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_helm_mode", "wander")
    yield success


# ---- the other consoles ------------------------------------------------------------
# These sit under a SEQ alongside the helm SEL, so every one runs each pass rather than
# the first success starving the rest. They were `delay_sim(10)` loops (engineering: 2),
# so at a 3-second brain pass science, weapons and comms all become MORE responsive than
# they are today; only engineering slows, and its work is a power/heat trim that does not
# need a 2-second cadence.

=== ai_player_science_select
" Selecting a science target
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
scan_range: 25000
```
    ap_foe = closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, side_hostile_ships(BRAIN_AGENT_ID), scan_range)
    yield fail if ap_foe is None
    yield success if get_science_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) == ap_foe
    set_science_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_foe)
    # Fire the real select ROUTE as well, so //select/science runs exactly as it would
    # for a crew member. That is the difference between exercising the console code and
    # merely writing the selection key.
    follow_route_select_science(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_foe)
    yield success


=== ai_player_comms
" Working the comms console
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
hail_range: 10000
```
    ap_foe = closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, side_hostile_ships(BRAIN_AGENT_ID), hail_range)
    yield fail if ap_foe is None
    ap_rid = to_id(ap_foe)
    if get_comms_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) != ap_rid:
        set_comms_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_rid)
        follow_route_select_comms(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_rid)

    # Taunt with the line an intel scan reveals, once per target - the wrong line does
    # not enrage their fleet, which is the point of taunting at all.
    ap_taunts = get_inventory_value(ap_rid, "taunt_data")
    ap_done = get_inventory_value(ap_rid, "taunt_attempted", False)
    ap_taunted = BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("comms_taunted_target", 0)
    if ap_taunts is not None and not ap_done and ap_taunted != ap_rid:
        ap_trait = get_inventory_value(ap_rid, "taunt_trait", 0)
        if ap_trait < len(ap_taunts):
            BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("comms_taunted_target", ap_rid)
            ap_line = ap_taunts[ap_trait]
            ap_taunt_data = ~~{"COMMS_ORIGIN_ID": BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "COMMS_SELECTED_ID": ap_rid, "data": ap_line, "select_right": True}~~
            task_schedule(handle_comms_taunt_raider_select, ap_taunt_data)

    # Shields down: demand surrender. The LM handler rolls the chance and reports it.
    ap_asked = BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("comms_surrender_target", 0)
    if ap_asked != ap_rid and not has_role(ap_rid, "surrendered") and not has_role(ap_rid, "never_surrender"):
        if autoplay_shields_down(to_blob(ap_rid)):
            BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("comms_surrender_target", ap_rid)
            ap_surr_data = ~~{"COMMS_ORIGIN_ID": BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "COMMS_SELECTED_ID": ap_rid}~~
            task_schedule(handle_comms_raider_surrender, ap_surr_data)
    yield success


=== ai_player_weapons_doctrine
" Choosing a weapon
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
engage_range: 10000
```
    # Ammo-aware ladder, unchanged from the loop version: the choice is the interesting
    # part and retuning it here would make the A/B compare two different bots.
    ap_foes = side_hostile_ships(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    ap_foe = closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_foes, engage_range)
    if ap_foe is None:
        # Nothing hostile: beams on a wreck still salvage it.
        ap_wreck = closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, role("wreck"), engage_range)
        yield fail if ap_wreck is None
        ap_wid = to_id(ap_wreck)
        if get_weapons_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) != ap_wid:
            set_weapons_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_wid)
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_weapon_choice", "beams_wreck")
        yield success

    ap_rid = to_id(ap_foe)
    if get_weapons_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) != ap_rid:
        set_weapons_selection(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_rid)

    # AOE weapons need a clear field: a friendly inside the blast is the reason to hold.
    ap_friends = side_allied_members(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) & broad_test_around(ap_rid, 3000, 3000, 0x30)
    ap_friends = ap_friends - {BRAIN_AGENT_ID}
    ap_cluster = ap_foes & broad_test_around(ap_rid, 2000, 2000, 0x30)
    ap_choice = autoplay_weapon_choice(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_rid, ap_foe.distance, len(ap_cluster), len(ap_friends) == 0, autoplay_shields_down(to_blob(ap_rid)), BRAIN_AGENT.get_inventory_value("opener_target", 0), SETTINGS.get("AUTO_PLAY", {}).get("standoff", 5000))
    BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("ap_weapon_choice", ap_choice)

    if ap_choice == "opener":
        # A multi-second scripted volley belongs in a task, not a leaf - a leaf that
        # awaits is left running while the next pass starts another. The flag is what
        # stops it being re-launched every pass.
        BRAIN_AGENT.set_inventory_value("opener_target", ap_rid)
        ap_open_data = ~~{"_ship_id": BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "target_id": ap_rid}~~
        task_schedule(automated_player_engage_opener, ap_open_data)
    elif ap_choice != "none":
        fire_torpedo(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ap_choice)
    yield success


=== ai_player_engineer_power
" Balancing power and coolant
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/player
```
    # Overpower the drive and weapons, back off as the tank drains, and hold anything
    # that is running hot. Then pour coolant on the hottest systems first.
    #
    # NOTE: the mock does not populate `eng_control_label` at all, so this does nothing
    # headless - the same is true of the loop version it replaces. It is engine-only
    # behaviour and a headless PASS says nothing about it either way.
    autoplay_set_power_plan(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, SETTINGS.get("AUTO_PLAY", {}).get("overpower", 1.5))
    autoplay_spend_coolant(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    yield success
